Authority is scoped: different subjects may have different authoritative sources without duplication. A draft issue or agent suggestion does not override an accepted requirement; implementation is evidence of actual behavior, and a discrepancy with the agreed requirement is reported, not silently normalized. An external authority remains authoritative even when it cannot be fetched; record the gap instead of fabricating its contents.
